1
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:05,000
The Chimera has multiple attributes.

2
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:08,620
A head of fire, a body of
earth, and a tail of water.

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:12,197
I'm guessing it'll break
out of the ice pretty soon.

4
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:16,300
You and I are about to undertake
our first Herculean labor of love.

5
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:21,357
We'll start with the head.

6
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:25,097
Your fire alone won't damage it much, so
I'll give you some backup with my water.

7
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,177
Will that be enough?

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:29,517
Even a combined attack will leave us
vulnerable to its water-based tail.

9
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:31,071
I've got a plan for that.

10
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:38,173
The plan has already been set in motion.

11
00:00:39,040 --> 00:00:40,452
Are you sure about this?

12
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:43,798
If we want to be together,
we have to take this risk.

13
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,400
I understand.

14
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,637
But it will take me some time
to prepare for such an endeavor.

15
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:50,779
I'll buy you all the time you need.

16
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:53,139
This plan requires me to trust you.

17
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:54,920
It sure does.

18
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:10,380
You're having second thoughts
because of Miss Claire. Yes.

19
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:11,810
Oh, no.

20
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:13,380
It just...

21
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:23,785
Time to play some cat-imax,
you big dumb kitty!

22
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:28,470
That's Ray!

23
00:01:28,553 --> 00:01:30,100
But where's Miss Claire?

24
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,560
Right into our trap!

25
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:07,700
Now freeze!

26
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:11,660
Alright, you're up, Ms.

27
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:12,590
Claire!

28
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:23,680
Honestly, you act as if it
were just another spell.

29
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,800
As I've told you once before,

30
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:30,808
this technique is exponentially
more powerful than my others.

31
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:36,237
If my aim falters in the slightest,
then the spell will strike you as well.

32
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:37,261
I'm not worried.

33
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,980
I know you can do this, Miss Claire.

34
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,590
Light.

35
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,110
Magic!

36
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:49,810
Magic! Rain!

37
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:23,440
I won't be able to stay
by her side anymore.

38
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:35,340
But at least I know that
Miss Claire won't be alone.

39
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:54,390
No, ain't you?

40
00:03:54,473 --> 00:03:57,517
I know, no, you have pride
What you want? All you want?

41
00:03:57,600 --> 00:04:01,237
Say that again All I want, only you?

42
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,877
Don't you know what you want?

43
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:04,037
No, you're not alone.

44
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:07,157
If you don't even though even though you
don't believe you you're only only this?

45
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,077
You're dead, right?

46
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,397
You're not so happy?

47
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:10,757
I want to go ahead!

48
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:11,670
How long you're not?

49
00:04:11,753 --> 00:04:12,583
You're a true self.

50
00:04:12,666 --> 00:04:14,660
Your sending me? It's real! I'm all right.

51
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:16,637
I'm out!

52
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:20,317
You're not!

53
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,517
I'm out!

54
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,457
You're fire!

55
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:25,217
You are too long!

56
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,737
People don't like to see me.

57
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:31,840
I don't like to see you.
Keep on the feelings!

58
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:35,557
So let's go!

59
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:37,197
Now right now!

60
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:39,037
I'm going to play.

61
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:41,220
I have a choice.

62
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,889
I'm going to be one thing.

63
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,840
From my heart!

64
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:48,370
Let's go!

65
00:04:48,453 --> 00:04:49,283
Let's go!

66
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,900
We actually pulled it off, Miss Claire!

67
00:05:15,780 --> 00:05:18,257
Indeed, we're fortunate
things unfolded as they did.

68
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:19,920
Honestly, what chaos?

69
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:21,620
Truly impressive.

70
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:26,480
I mean for a spoiled little
rich girl. Miss Claire!

71
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,920
Prince Dane!

72
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,157
You're bleeding.

73
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,070
Just a scratch.

74
00:05:39,153 --> 00:05:40,375
She barely grazed me.

75
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,140
Well, well, well.

76
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:47,597
If it isn't the failure,
Prince. Who are you?

77
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,640
Were you the one behind all this?

78
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:57,180
My initial aim was to eliminate as
many of the nobility as possible,

79
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:59,399
but this exceeds those aspirations.

80
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,700
Savor your demise.

81
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:06,040
He got away. I stayed!

82
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:07,681
Are you alright?

83
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:08,977
What did he do to you?

84
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:09,960
Look, his arm.

85
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:26,280
Prince Tain, stay with us, please!

86
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,497
He's infected with a new type of poison.

87
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:29,677
Stand back, Miss Claire.

88
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:30,940
I'll neutralize it.

89
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:58,179
Looks like he's gonna be all right.

90
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:00,480
You were able to save him? Yep.

91
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,480
Thank goodness.

92
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:12,400
It was Cantarella, a deadly poison
from the newer Empire. What?

93
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:15,328
Is that where the
intruder was from as well?

94
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,640
Yeah, most likely.

95
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:20,997
Whenever there's a major conflict
in this world, the Noor Empire,

96
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:23,537
Bauer's sworn enemy, is usually behind it.

97
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:26,417
They first use Cantorella
in the game's later stages,

98
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:29,737
and it's up to the heroine
to come up with the antidote.

99
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:34,840
Thanks to that, I knew how to counteract
it, but still... Rey! I'm here! What?

100
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,630
Fade?

101
00:07:36,713 --> 00:07:38,501
Hey, what the hell happened here?

102
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,340
Cut with a poison blade.

103
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,780
But I neutralized it.

104
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,857
Still, it wouldn't hurt
to take him to a doctor.

105
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:47,117
I swear...

106
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:50,240
He just had to charge in by himself.

107
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,230
That idiot.

108
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:59,352
Looks like they've arrested them already.

109
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:08,950
Lene...

110
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:20,260
And just like that, the whole
incident was brought to an end.

111
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:28,477
The protests have ended, and it seems
the commoner movement is fading out.

112
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:31,437
We also know that Deed wasn't
responsible for the assault,

113
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:34,337
and the Nahr Empire was behind
it all from the beginning.

114
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:38,596
I can't believe we played right into
an enemy nation's hands like that.

115
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:42,960
Will the entire Oruso family be punished?

116
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:44,330
Probably.

117
00:08:44,413 --> 00:08:47,964
Even if they were manipulated,
that doesn't change what happened.

118
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:50,757
They've been relieved of duties
pertaining to Magic Stones,

119
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:53,817
and they're presently awaiting
the Kingdom's decision.

120
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:54,730
Decision?

121
00:08:54,813 --> 00:08:56,151
What will happen to them?

122
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:04,093
What Master Lambert and Lene did
amounts to treason against the Kingdom.

123
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:06,574
No escaping the death penalty for that.

124
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,078
Oh, I almost forgot to tell you two.

125
00:09:09,980 --> 00:09:10,810
Uh...

126
00:09:10,893 --> 00:09:13,297
Rumor has it that you both
will be receiving a reward.

127
00:09:13,380 --> 00:09:15,837
A reward? Whatever for? Well,

128
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:17,957
uncovering the mastermind
of an evil plot and

129
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:20,017
thwarting the plans of
our enemies for starters.

130
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:22,757
And then there was the part
where Rey saved Thane's life.

131
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:25,697
It's safe to say you'll be
summoned to the royal palace soon.

132
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:28,437
Father would like to thank
the both of you personally.

133
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:30,377
But we let the culprit get away.

134
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:31,820
Why would... Whoa!

135
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,515
Isn't that something?

136
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:35,477
We'll gladly take what he has to offer!

137
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,560
Won't we, mister?

138
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:37,997
What is wrong with you?

139
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,080
Take a breath and listen to me.

140
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,237
I understand.

141
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,908
We shall give it our
very best effort, then.

142
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:04,820
Will you just sit down?

143
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,797
I can't relax with all that fidgeting.

144
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:09,840
Sorry, I'm afraid I'm gonna
wrinkle my new outfit.

145
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:14,860
My lady, thank you for generously
bestowing these sweet thoughts upon me.

146
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:15,930
Oh, please.

147
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:18,137
It's not as though I did it for your sake.

148
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:21,637
I'd be the one facing humiliation if
you showed up looking like a vagrant.

149
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:25,137
You can act quite all you want, but
we both know it was a gesture of love.

150
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:26,691
Will you kindly be quiet?

151
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:31,916
Honestly, it'd actually be rather
striking if you kept your mouth shut.

152
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:32,950
Huh?

153
00:10:33,033 --> 00:10:34,100
I didn't say a word.

154
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:40,060
Miss Claire Francois, Miss
Ray Taylor, please follow me.

155
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:41,866
His Majesty will see you now.

156
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:00,440
Please, lift your heads.

157
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,857
It has come to my attention
that you two were the ones

158
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:12,116
responsible for thwarting
the incident at the Academy.

159
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:18,420
I am also told that you
saved my son's life.

160
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,757
For this, I owe you a great debt.

161
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:23,193
Name your wish, and it shall be granted.

162
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:27,460
Your Majesty,

163
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:32,437
thank you for your generous offer, and
for graciously granting us this audience.

164
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:34,677
This is entirely up to her.

165
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,317
As much as I'd like to
help, I'm a commoner.

166
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,459
I can't speak directly to the king.

167
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:44,857
Regarding our reward, there is but
one thing we would like to ask of you.

168
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:46,293
And what might that be?

169
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:48,717
A plea, sire.

170
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:50,900
Here we go, the moment of truth.

171
00:11:52,260 --> 00:11:56,420
I beseech your majesty to
spare the lives of the Orusos!

172
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:10,504
It was my understanding that the Orasols
were the primary culprits in this matter.

173
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:14,857
Are you truly suggesting that I
reduce the sentence for their crimes?

174
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:15,940
Yes, Your Grace.

175
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:20,220
I humbly request that you show
mercy and grant them a pardon.

176
00:12:22,100 --> 00:12:22,930
Interesting.

177
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:24,360
Salas, what say you?

178
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,740
It would be difficult.

179
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:29,711
Ours is a system of reward and punishment.

180
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:33,259
I see no justification for
commuting their sentence.

181
00:12:34,560 --> 00:12:36,140
This isn't going well.

182
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:40,240
Your Majesty, I implore you
to think of the Oroso's trade.

183
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:43,735
In the past, they have
contributed much to our economy,

184
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:46,687
particularly to the
business of magic stones.

185
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:51,196
Surely such contributions support
their case for clemency, do they not?

186
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:55,020
You have a point.

187
00:12:55,340 --> 00:12:59,737
Is it truly infeasible to commute their
sentence in light of their services, Solace?

188
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:03,040
Indeed, we acknowledge the
contributions you named.

189
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,997
But collusion with a foreign
power and plotting harm

190
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:09,198
against the kingdom are
crimes of the gravest nature.

191
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,980
Nothing less than execution will suffice.

192
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:14,800
And so it shall be done.

193
00:13:15,220 --> 00:13:17,279
Please present a different request.

194
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,780
Your Majesty,

195
00:13:22,160 --> 00:13:26,689
if I'm not too late, I'd like to ask
that you consider granting their appeal.

196
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:31,720
You may approach, Thane.

197
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:41,580
This turmoil stemmed from unrest
and conflict between the classes.

198
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:45,317
The commoners rebelled against
what they saw as an injustice,

199
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,580
a wrong done to one of their
own in favor of a noble.

200
00:13:50,260 --> 00:13:53,857
If your majesty does not take
steps to demonstrate equality,

201
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:56,480
we may face this again in the future.

202
00:13:57,140 --> 00:13:57,970
Hmm.

203
00:13:58,053 --> 00:14:01,760
And you believe that sparing the
Orusos will help improve relations?

204
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:02,730
Absolutely.

205
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,360
If I may, your majesty, Prince Thane.

206
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,797
There is widespread suspicion
that the Orusos were the

207
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:11,477
ones who founded the commoner
movement in the first place.

208
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:16,157
If they are spared, the nobles whose
children were endangered will not accept it.

209
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:19,797
But people of all backgrounds
contribute to our nation's magic.

210
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:23,657
Not only nobles, but the common people who
make up the majority of the population.

211
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:27,940
If you do not wish for your meritocracy
to be called an empty promise,

212
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,299
please reconsider.

213
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:33,460
I am prepared to make my final judgment.

214
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:42,400
The Oroso family will be
exiled from this kingdom.

215
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:47,780
Your Majesty, with all due
- I'll have no dissent.

216
00:14:48,700 --> 00:14:49,530
Apologies.

217
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:54,344
The details of their banishment
shall be disclosed in due course.

218
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:59,180
Claire Francois, Ray
Taylor, you are dismissed.

219
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,020
We did it!

220
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:13,768
Stealing my words, are you?

221
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,960
We just share the same brain cell.

222
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:19,057
I'm in your head and pretty soon I'm
gonna find my way into your heart.

223
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:19,980
You will not!

224
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,057
And I share no part of
your demented brain!

225
00:15:22,140 --> 00:15:23,637
Then let's share our love instead!

226
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:24,837
You just proved my point!

227
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:26,517
We did it! We did it!

228
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:27,997
We really, really did it!

229
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:33,100
Yay, Miss Claire!

230
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:53,922
There they are.

231
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,677
All of the Oruso's
possessions were confiscated,

232
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:01,997
and the entire family was
banished to a neighboring land.

233
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:05,877
So do you think all of them will find
a way to survive out there in the Alps?

234
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:09,197
I've heard that Bartley, their
family's head, is remarkably competent.

235
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:13,317
I'm sure they'll secure sufficient
means to put food on the table at least.

236
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:15,277
But what about Lene and Lambert?

237
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:17,419
The two of them are being disowned.

238
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:22,700
And even so, as long as they're
alive, they still have hope.

239
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:32,510
Lene!

240
00:16:48,260 --> 00:16:49,960
Oh, Ray, Miss Claire.

241
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,497
Someone wanted to come
and say goodbye to you.

242
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,417
I wanted to do nothing of the sort.

243
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:57,197
You practically dragged me here.

244
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,110
Don't lie.

245
00:16:58,193 --> 00:16:59,737
I could see the longing in your eyes.

246
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:00,650
Now go on.

247
00:17:00,733 --> 00:17:02,777
You just do your thing
and pretend I'm not here.

248
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:04,566
Believe me, I constantly try.

249
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:09,204
Please forgive me for laughing.

250
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:12,026
It's nice to know some
things haven't changed.

251
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:18,120
Lene, how are you?

252
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:25,837
They could easily have executed us.

253
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:29,397
Considering what we were accused
of, no one would have batted an eye.

254
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:31,857
But now we have a chance to start over.

255
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:34,411
Because you two cared enough to intervene.

256
